MoBetta: ntdll: Start i386 processes under the x87sidecar cooperatively.

Port of athei/wine f837e313f79eb721329314e371fd2bdc41f21186 by Alexander
Theißen (https://github.com/athei/wine/commit/f837e313f), without its
compatdb.so parts. Upstream asks its own compatdb.so (compatdb_query_x87,
compatdb_query_env) whether to attach and which env to set, and loads it
before ntdll is initialized behind a compatdb_preinit_query() guard. CrossOver
26.3 ships cxcompatdb.so, which has neither query nor guard, so MoBetta drops
that machinery and always takes upstream's "no opinion" answer: every i386
process is started under the sidecar when there is one. coop_proto.h is
upstream's copy, wire-identical to x87sidecar's rosetta_loader/src/coop_proto.h.

Stock Rosetta runs each x87 instruction through software 80-bit routines in
libRosettaRuntime; in WoW 3.3.5a they take about 65% of the main thread.
For an i386 target, preloader_exec re-execs as
`x87sidecar --cooperative <loader> <args>`, and __wine_main hands the task and
main-thread ports to the sidecar over the bootstrap service named in
X87_SIDECAR_BOOTSTRAP, waits for its reply and invalidates the i-cache for the
code it patched. Any failure prints a "RUNNING WITHOUT X87 ACCELERATION"
banner and continues on stock Rosetta. NtCreateUserProcess decides the same
for a child before fork.

The sidecar is ROSETTA_X87_PATH if set (an empty value turns it off), else
bin_dir/x87sidecar if executable there (x86_64 macOS builds only), else none.

preloader_exec only goes through the sidecar when argv[1], the loader, exists.
Upstream gets that from a check in get_alternate_wineloader() (part of
athei/wine 1287daf360); CX 26.3 returns i386-unix/wine there even on a
wow64-only install like MoBetta's, which would hang the launch in the
handshake. Checking in preloader_exec keeps stock start-up unchanged.

